              "label": "< 50 years",
              "children": [
                {
                  "label": "migraine/vasospasm",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "label": "most common cause",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "label": "transient homonymous hemianopia is frequently misperceived by the patient as a monocular visual loss in the eye with the temporal field deficit"
